2763, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16123366</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ozcan U, Yilmaz E, Ozcan L, Furuhashi M, Vaillancourt E, Smith RO, Gorgun CZ, Hotamisligil GS: Chemical chaperones reduce ER stress and restore glucose homeostasis in a mouse model of type 2 diabetes. <source>Science</source> <volume>313</volume>: <fpage>1137</fpage>&#x02013;1140, <year>2006</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16931765</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">Urano F, Wang X, Bertolotti A, Zhang Y, Chung P, Harding HP, Ron D: Coupling of stress in the ER to activation of JNK protein kinases by transmembrane protein kinase IRE1. <source>Science</source> <volume>287</volume>: <fpage>664</fpage>&#x02013;666, <year>2000</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10650002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Dorner AJ, Wasley LC, Kaufman RJ: Overexpression of GRP78 mitigates stress induction of glucose regulated proteins and blocks secretion of selective proteins in Chinese hamster ovary cells. <source>Embo J</source> <volume>11</volume>: <fpage>1563</fpage>&#x02013;1571, <year>1992</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1373378</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal">Gotoh T, Oyadomari S, Mori K, Mori M: Nitric oxide-induced apoptosis in RAW 264.7 macrophages is mediated by endoplasmic reticulum stress pathway involving ATF6 and CHOP. <source>J Biol Chem</source> <volume>277</volume>: <fpage>12343</fpage>&#x02013;12350, <year>2002</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11805088</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal">Maytin EV, Ubeda M, Lin JC, Habener JF: Stress-inducible transcription factor CHOP/gadd153 induces apoptosis in mammalian cells via p38 kinase-dependent and -independent mechanisms. <source>Exp Cell Res</source> <volume>